Vehicle breakdown.- In case a vehicle with more than two wheels has broken down at a place where it can be recognised in time as a stationary obstacle,-
i. the hazard warning lights of the vehicle shall be switched on immediately;
ii. on highways and major roads with fast speed, reflective traffic warning triangles shall be placed at a distance of fifty meters behind the broken-down vehicle; and iii. if there is a bend on the road where the vehicle is parked, reflective traffic warning triangles shall be placed before the bend."
